question:
Given a positive integer $n$, find all pairs of positive integers $(x,y)$ such that
\begin{align*}
x^y+y^n&=x^n,\\
y^x+x^n&=y^n+2023.
\end{align*}
Determine all such pairs $(x,y)$ and the corresponding values of $n$.

Let \[g(x) =
\begin{cases}
x^3-x &\text{if } x<a, \\
\sin{x} &\text{if }x\ge{a}.
\end{cases}
\]If the graph $y=g(x)$ is continuous and differentiable at $x=a$, find the smallest possible value of $a$.

